	(text "Drop-in alternative to variant A (report 4.5): same magnet, same tail, same firmware bus - only the\nsensor changes. Real Western distribution, so it is the sourcing hedge for the MT6701." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 164 27 0) (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left top)) (uuid "202b5136-8ddc-4f91-942c-61acc209a3f7"))
	(text "3.3 V mode (ams Figure 14): VDD5V and VDD3V3\ntied together, 100 nF. Range 3.0-3.6 V; our\n3.1 V rail is inside it (switch R_on <= 0.5 R).\n\nDIR to GND = angle increases clockwise.\nFirmware normalises direction per variant.\n\nTEST (A2, C1, E2) to GND - required.\nPGO left open (internal pull-up = option A).\nOUT (PWM) unused. NC balls: do not connect.\n\nFirmware tells the variants apart by I2C\naddress: 0x06 = MT6701, 0x40 = AS5600L." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 280 50 0) (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left top)) (uuid "d511c6ba-6942-49d1-beb3-2cc7adb3110a"))
	(text "C1 at the VDD balls. C4 10 uF is only needed while OTP-programming (3.3-3.5 V on the fixture).\n12-bit = 0.088 deg per step, ~170 steps per 15-degree detent." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 164 126 0) (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left top)) (uuid "db257949-c051-49a4-8075-cb933b248dbb"))
	(rectangle (start 15 150) (end 200 262) (stroke (width 0.254) (type dash) (color 72 72 72 1)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "804e3fa7-41f7-4f4f-838b-2d00052e0f4f"))
	(text "C · Wake-on-rotation — 2 x DRV5032DU Hall latches (always on)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 16.5 151.5 0) (effects (font (size 2.0 2.0) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "bb0e9c70-af72-44cb-b4a9-4458cdbfee49"))
